{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>Pericope.</b> Bread for the poor — to her household. Her household, that is, she does not fear the snow falling on the earth, for every one of her household is clothed in scarlet of double, or her entire household is clothed in doubles; shesh is of the linen kind, and argaman is of the dyed kind, and it is red."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {0 "The comment begins as a cross-reference note to verse 15 (bread for the poor → her household), then addresses verse 21 (snow, scarlet/doubles). 'Scarlet of double' renders כרמיל שני hyper-literally; the syntax and meaning of this phrase are uncertain. 'Shesh' and 'argaman' are left untranslated as technical terms per the voice rules for biblical Hebrew terms that Ibn Ezra himself is glossing."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:25:53.660496723Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}